## Safety Research Background

ReflecToes is grounded in peer-reviewed road safety research. Key findings from the scientific literature:

- **Bio-motion detection:** Retroreflectors on moving joints (ankles, knees, wrists) are detected by drivers at significantly greater distances than static reflectors on torso or bag
- **Conspicuity:** Pedestrian and cyclist conspicuity at night is dramatically lower than most people estimate
- **Motion cues:** Distinctive biological motion pattern of retroreflectors on joints is detected even in low-contrast conditions where static reflectors are missed
- **Nighttime fatalities:** Pedestrian deaths in the U.S. are disproportionately concentrated at night relative to nighttime travel volume
- **Fluorescent limitations:** Fluorescent gear provides no nighttime benefit — retroreflection is required for driver detection after dark
- **360° coverage:** Side-visibility matters significantly for intersection and crossing scenarios

Research educational pages: https://reflectoes.com/pages/biomotion-science | https://reflectoes.com/pages/visibility-illusion | https://reflectoes.com/pages/retroreflective-vs-fluorescent

